{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1537401-what-s-your-favorite-family-and-lineage","id":1537401,"title":"What's your favorite Family and Lineage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-15T10:02:06-07:00","id":1537401,"title":"What's your favorite Family and Lineage?","content":"While I'm aware we don't know <i>that </i>much about all thirty curseborne splits yet, we do know at least a little bit each of them. I'll list them in the next post.<br /> please tell me about you favorite <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T10:05:08-07:00","id":1537402,"title":"","content":"The Dead. Yearns for a sensation that never quite satisfies.<br /> <br /> --The Shades. They are about sadness and misery. omens of ill fortune. They seek out the guilty and &quot;deserving&quot; of misery...and give it to them! --The Wardens. Cult mentality around their Family. Consider themselves protectors, so they seek out desperation. They just *might* cause problems in order to fix them.<br /> --The Furies. &quot;The 'fuck around and find out' group.&quot; Their urge is vengeance. Ghost Rider.<br /> --The Poltergeists. All about fear. Not just jump scares; they want dread. Will often try to use their powers to teach valuable lessons...but that's just trying to make the best of a bad situation.<br /> --The Mavens. Exhilaration and thrill. Can be pleasant and joyful, but can be dangerous and escalating &quot;thrill seeking.&quot; Pushing someone out of a window and basking in the &quot;rush&quot; of free falling (to their death) would count.<br /> --The Zeds. A bit different. They yearn less for an emotion than for &quot;endings.&quot; Closure and finality. Easiest way to do this? Kill people! Literally a company of assassins.<br /> <br /> The Hungry. Never satisfied when eating.<br /> The Black Hearts: found family made up of those who broke away from their original family's feeding restrictions. They eat emotions. They can be anarchic and a little bit &quot;mercenary.&quot; Also called Dhampir.<br /> --Gaki: Necromancers, who can bargain with AND eat ghosts.<br /> --Heirs: Those who Rule the rulers. likely to foster and build community, but likely to do so for selfish reasons. Rich.<br /> --House Bathory: Hedonists. &quot;A little bloody and a little fighty, because you need to spill blood to bathe in it.&quot; Pretentious, believe themselves to be descended from royalty, but don't actually claim leadership.<br /> --Iscariots: claim to be descended from Judas Iscariot, the betrayer of Jesus. Rebels with a cause. will fight for what's &quot;right,&quot; but may be a bit delusional about just how &quot;right&quot; they are. Would rather &quot;burn it all down&quot; than let things stand as they are.<br /> --Vorare: Infernalists. Pacts with Demons. Eat Souls. Driven to make the world a better place (for the most part.) Desire to break their Curse<br /> --Ascetics: Knowledge hoarders/brokers. Pyramid scheme, knowledge is tithed UP, but rarely trickles back down. Not TECHNICALLY structured lie a pyramid, but still functions like an MLM","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T10:05:38-07:00","id":1537403,"title":"","content":"The Primal. Fights the creature inside that will kill those you love most. --Eight Hands: Spider shifters. They keep secrets, weave webs of conspiracy and networks of informants.<br /> --Get of Lyka: Wolf shifters. They're cursed by anger, and made a deal with the Creature to get back at an oppressor.<br /> --Hydes: Born from Dr. Jekyll and his desire to bottle the creature and use it to his own purposes. Now they become inhuman creatures and can bottle their spells for later use.<br /> --Raptors: Bird/reptile shifters. They seek the truth. Claim to be the oldest of all the Primal. They tend to be planners, calculating and brutal. (They mention being able to turn into a dragon.)<br /> --Spawn of Vodnik: Aquatic shifters (frogs, merfolk, fish, sharks). They are sneaky, fighty, and cultivate a provincial attitude so that people will underestimate them.<br /> --Sphinx: Cat shifters. Cursed by pride. They act like cats in that they act as rulers, and like to &quot;play with their prey.&quot; They are much more sinister than the rest of the families.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T10:06:43-07:00","id":1537404,"title":"","content":"The Outcasts. Outcasts are people who's distant ancestors were exiled from the Outside - from heaven, hell, and everything between. Could be anything. Doesn't have to be blood relationship - it could actually pass onto an adopted child - you need to have a familial relation, even if not biologically.<br /> --Battleground Angels - Militant group who actively go into battlegrounds and fight the entities therein. Kind of like a resistance group?<br /> --Chimera - People who got Cursed for attempting to become gods by opening gates into Outside. Don't look human, have scorpion tails, weird eyes, horns, etc.<br /> --Nephilim - Travelers. Big emphasis on collecting secrets and traveling Outsides to gain information. Big emphasis on family, moreso than usual.<br /> --Keepers of the Broken Vine - Decided that, as long as they're trapped in mundane world, going to make it a better place. Trying to foster a natural world, create life, communing with nature.<br /> --Munificents - You should try to redeem yourself and become more of a spirit being again. Treat others better than they've been treated. Giving other people what they want. Grant other people's wishes as well - more like an angel or non-evil genie.<br /> --League of Hidden Crossroads - Devil's bargain guys. A family of choice, sign up by coming together and all about tempting people. Wandering through life and being the person people meet at crossroads in life where they offer a choice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T10:07:34-07:00","id":1537405,"title":"","content":"The Sorcerers. Addicted to magic, and unable to kick the habit.<br /> -Archivists. The Sacrifice secrets. They hoard secrets. Secrets can be Sacrificed by &quot;spilling the beans,' so it's not really a secret anymore, is it? Or by actually destroying the knowledge. They don't have to be &quot;your&quot; secrets! An Archivist could betray a friend by telling theirs secrets...or ruin an antagonists plans by erasing the memory of a vile ritual or spell from existence.<br /> --The Faceless. They Sacrifice recognition or acclaim. They will pull off a daring heist, con, assassination, or the like. As long as no one -NO ONE- knows they did it, they have Sacrificed that recognition or acclaim. It has to be something illegal, as the risk of getting caught is part of the Sacrifice.<br /> --The Network. A &quot;tried and true&quot; pyramid scheme. They Sacrifice connections to other people. They network with other people, and bring more and more into their group, cultivating relationships...for the express purpose of &quot;burning&quot; them up to fuel their magic. (There are &quot;very strict rules&quot; against doing this to other Accursed...but &quot;there's always someone...&quot;<br /> --The Premier. A wealthy family, they collect fame, wealth, and power. They Sacrifice time and energy. They volunteer and promote charities a lot. It *is* a Sacrifice! They do not have much free time or personal space or privacy! And the family isn't &quot;nobody has to work a day in their lives&quot; wealthy, just &quot;everybody has a pretty reliable safety net&quot; wealthy.<br /> --The Reeves. They Sacrifice life death. But! It is very important to them to do it in harmony with nature. Weeding a garden, cutting back overgrowth, culling a herd all Sacrifice life. Saving a life or working a suicide hotline are examples of Sacrificing death. Reeves honor the natural cycle of life and death.<br /> --The Unburdened. They Sacrifice all their worldly possessions. If they get something, they either share it with their Family or Sacrifice it. Admittedly, access to magic can make living without &quot;things&quot; a somewhat more practical (and even comfortable) lifestyle choice!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T10:52:24-07:00","id":1537408,"title":"","content":"I am really excited about the Hungry but I'm not a huge fan of equating the hedonists all with an RL serial killer.<br /> <br /> Still, all of the Hungry intrigue me.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea the rebels are the Iscariots, Whether intentional or not, it's a nice little &quot;take that&quot; to a certain RPG's use of rebellious Christian mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T11:18:23-07:00","id":1537411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1537401-what-s-your-favorite-family-and-lineage?p=1537408#post1537408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am really excited about the Hungry but I'm not a huge fan of equating the hedonists all with an RL serial killer.<br /> <br /> Still, all of the Hungry intrigue me.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea the rebels are the Iscariots, Whether intentional or not, it's a nice little &quot;take that&quot; to a certain RPG's use of rebellious Christian mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, I like the Gaki","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 06-15-2024, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T14:38:02-07:00","id":1537432,"title":"","content":"I currently am on Raptors, Reeves, and Munificents - Raptors because they emphasize one can be a combat beast while still having a brain, Reeves for the dark take on White Mages that are still clearly White Mages (and also Euthanatos), and Munificents for the sheer &quot;screw your darkness, I'm an angel&quot; chutzpah (followed closely by Battlefield Angels, but Munificents aren't even &quot;cold justice&quot; angels).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T08:03:48-07:00","id":1537489,"title":"","content":"Nephilim and the League of Hidden Crossroads for me. I guess Outcasts appeal to me.<br /> <br /> I fell out of WoD before Chronicles really became a thing. Let's see if Curseborne can draw me back into a Modern/Urban Horror RPG again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T11:13:44-07:00","id":1537506,"title":"","content":"Hey Nic, quick question: I assume you got the Families from the Curseborne Panel? They didn't get into the weeds in the Ashcan, so I'm curious where we got those cited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T12:33:20-07:00","id":1537516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1537401-what-s-your-favorite-family-and-lineage?p=1537506#post1537506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Nic, quick question: I assume you got the Families from the Curseborne Panel? They didn't get into the weeds in the Ashcan, so I'm curious where we got those cited.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe they come from what was discussed in the various character creation videos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T12:34:00-07:00","id":1537517,"title":"","content":"Keepers of the Broken Vine appeal to me. I got Raptor in the quiz.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T14:19:56-07:00","id":1537525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1537401-what-s-your-favorite-family-and-lineage?p=1537506#post1537506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Nic, quick question: I assume you got the Families from the Curseborne Panel? They didn't get into the weeds in the Ashcan, so I'm curious where we got those cited.</div> </div> </div> </div>Howdy there Kelly! they were compiled from the charge videos danielle lauzon did with the players of the actual play that showed up at the opp con<br /> EDIT:Compiled mostly by Corbin from the discord","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T16:34:46-07:00","id":1537730,"title":"","content":"Pretty interested by the variety of sorcerers, primal and hungries (although I would like to know the feeding restriction that are yet to be mentioned for some families).<br /> <br /> I feel that more details on what kind of spirits or other &quot;thing&quot; outcasts can be. Their families, outside of chimeras, sounds like more organisation's rather than nature. <br /> <br /> As for the dead, Seeking the guilty, seeking desesperation, vengeance, teaching a lesson for fears sake, killing to cause a conclusion,<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200boutside of the maven, the families focus sounds far too much similar to each others.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-23T21:30:00-07:00","id":1542540,"title":"","content":"There are a number of families that seem cool to me.<br /> <br /> The one that excites me most at the moment are the Spawn of Vodnik. I see some cool elements from HP Lovecraft\u2019s writing - the Deep Ones. I like that they are secretive sneak collectors of lost relics or curiosities. I like that they tend to be providential, living in remote region away from prying eyes. I think it\u2019s cool that they are a literal family, I am seeing potential aspects of Revenants or the Addams family there. From the current information, they seem like the coolest family to me.<br /> <br /> I think that the Unburdened are really interesting as well. I like the idea of these hippie, anarchist, anti-materialists, who wander the land trying to make ends meet. Almost like magical mendicants.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T05:24:05-07:00","id":1542545,"title":"","content":"Currently I'm a fan of the Hungry, Bathorites and Vorare both appeal to me with Gaki being a wait and see how their necromancy works. My first character I made (using the character sheets someone shared here) is a Bathorite I reverse engineered the stars for from the Trashcan. <br /> <br /> I'm also very intrigued by Outsiders and Sorcerers but I need to see a lot more on them before I make a decision. I want to see more of the dead but I'm less excited for them. <br /> <br /> Strangely enough, Primals don't really appeal to me despite me my love of werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T10:26:46-07:00","id":1543013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1537401-what-s-your-favorite-family-and-lineage?p=1537408#post1537408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am really excited about the Hungry but I'm not a huge fan of equating the hedonists all with an RL serial killer.<br /> <br /> Still, all of the Hungry intrigue me.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea the rebels are the Iscariots, Whether intentional or not, it's a nice little &quot;take that&quot; to a certain RPG's use of rebellious Christian mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>what's the RPG? /gen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27963-jayng2183","name":"JayNg2183","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27963_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T15:06:42-07:00","id":1543030,"title":"","content":"So far Mavens, Munificents, and Keepers of the Broken Vine look best. None of the Sorcerer families look good to me. Archivists look possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}